# Website relation (explorations vs MCP)

## One capability, three presentations

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| Website exploration | Human textbook — pedagogy, widgets, curated examples |
| MCP docs `use/eips/eip-NNNN` | Human inspiration — what to ask an agent, Connect |
| Engine module + generic tools | Runtime — execute **caller-supplied** bytecode |

## Twin, not clone

- Same **core question** (e.g. “can Amsterdam run DUPN?”) — different **artifact**
- Website owns **interactive examples**; MCP owns **general execution**
- Do **not** replay exploration widget bytecode in the engine catalog
- Do **not** import from `website/src/explorations/` into this repo

## Cross-links (human docs only)

- Exploration → MCP docs: `/use/eips/eip-NNNN` (future website icon)
- MCP docs → exploration: feelyourprotocol.org route + EIP spec

## Adding exploration does not add MCP

The website `add-exploration` skill is out of scope for engine/gateway work unless explicitly requested. A new exploration without a runnable module does not appear in `describeCapabilities()`.
